        <gr str="4339">aright</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="32"> At the <gr str="319">last </gr>it <gr str="5391">biteth </gr>like a <gr str="5175">serpent</gr>, and <gr str="6567">stingeth </gr>like an <gr str="6848">adder</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="33"> Thine <gr str="5869">eyes </gr>shall <gr str="7200">behold </gr>strange <gr str="2114">women</gr>, and thine <gr str="3820">heart </gr>shall <gr str="1696">utter </gr>perverse <gr str="8419">things</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="34"> Yea, thou shalt <gr str="1961">be </gr>as he that lieth <gr str="7901">down </gr>in the <gr str="3820">midst </gr>of the <gr str="3220">sea</gr>, or as he that <gr str="7901">lieth </gr>upon the <gr str="7218">top </gr>of a <gr str="2260">mast</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="35"> They have <gr str="5221">stricken </gr>me, <STYLE css="color:#808080;font-style:italic"> shalt </STYLE>
